    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Model experiments have been conducted in a layered brittle coating bounded to a PMMA substrate to understand the influence of layer thickness and applied strain on joint spacing for sedimentary rocks. Limiting strains of fracture saturation are found for each thickness of the brittle coating. Different methods of spacing measurement for a poorly developed fracture set and a well developed set are compared. To distinguish a poorly developed set from a well developed set for bore hole data a simple method is suggested.",
